## [Types of NoSQL databases](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/choosing-an-aws-nosql-database/types-of-nosql-databases.md)

### [Understanding Amazon NoSQL data stores](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/choosing-an-aws-nosql-database/understanding-amazon-nosql-data-stores.md)

AWS provides the broadest selection of managed NoSQL databases, allowing you to save, grow, and innovate faster.

- [Amazon DynamoDB](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/choosing-an-aws-nosql-database/amazon-dynamodb.md): Amazon DynamoDB is a fully managed NoSQL database service.
- [Amazon Keyspaces (for Apache Cassandra)](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/choosing-an-aws-nosql-database/amazon-keyspaces.md): Amazon Keyspaces (for Apache Cassandra) (Amazon Keyspaces) is a fully managed, Apache Cassandra-compatible database service.
- [Amazon Neptune](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/choosing-an-aws-nosql-database/amazon-neptune.md): Amazon Neptune is a fully managed graph database service.
- [Amazon Timestream](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/choosing-an-aws-nosql-database/amazon-timestream.md): Amazon Timestream is a managed time series database.
- [Amazon ElastiCache](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/choosing-an-aws-nosql-database/amazon-elasticache.md): Amazon ElastiCache is a web service that makes it easy to deploy, operate, and scale an in-memory cache in the cloud.
- [Amazon DocumentDB](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/choosing-an-aws-nosql-database/amazon-documentdb.md): Amazon DocumentDB (with MongoDB compatibility) (Amazon DocumentDB) is a fully managed, scalable, and highly available document database service.
- [Amazon MemoryDB](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/choosing-an-aws-nosql-database/amazon-memorydb-for-redis.md): Amazon MemoryDB (MemoryDB) is a fully managed, in-memory database service.


